; Product fold — same accumulator-threading shape as expr-fold-sum
; but the body multiplies rather than adds, and the init is `1`
; (the multiplicative identity) rather than `0`. The pair of
; fixtures pins fold's "init must be applied as iteration-0 acc"
; semantics: a buggy implementation that started the accumulator
; at the wrong identity would produce wildly different results
; under multiplication vs addition.
(fold [acc x] 1 [1 2 3 4] (* acc x))
